{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508314-not-enough-werewolves-game-idea","id":508314,"title":"Not enough Werewolves [Game Idea]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-08T12:47:38-07:00","id":508314,"title":"Not enough Werewolves [Game Idea]","content":"I'm planning to ST a game in which Uratha are running thin - especially in the player's home town - so they have to make-do with enrolling extraordinary Wolf-Blooded into the hunt. Basically it would be a 2 Uratha 3 Wolf-Blooded game. Now the power-difference between Uratha and WB is a large gap and I don't want to simply drop 20 XP on my WB players to try and balance things so I need another way.<br /> <br /> Here are the ideas I had, but I wanted your oppinions on what would work and what would cause important problems.<br /> <br /> -Allow the WB with a corresponding tell the ability to cast Wolf Rites<br /> -Allow Supernatural Merits to the WB<br /> -Give free Auspice and Tribe merits to the WB<br /> -Allow buying Shadow Gifts to the WB after a succesful hunt<br /> <br /> I don't want to give them all of these options (because then why not simply make them werewolves) but some oppinions or alternative ideas would be greatly appreciated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T12:58:45-07:00","id":508342,"title":"","content":"I'd probably stick to the first two, and allow fetish and talen usage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-08-2015, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T13:07:15-07:00","id":508356,"title":"","content":"Yeah, opening up fetishes will give them a lot more bite. <br /> <br /> Maybe you could let wolf rites be learned by WBs that have one of the mystic tells <i>plus</i> one that lets them shapeshift or something. Like, they've got enough werewolf in them that whatever mystic block stops them from doing the wolf rites just... gives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T19:32:11-07:00","id":508641,"title":"","content":"It might not be pertinent to you, since I don't even know if you have the werewolf chroniclers guide, but with the new wolf-blooded rules the Jackals would work particularly well as an intermediate state between normal wolf-blooded and full werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T00:24:41-07:00","id":508808,"title":"","content":"Although you might need to consider a few things when porting them over. How does their primal urge work now? Do they use the new chart? How do the feeding restrictions work when they gain essence from <i>any</i> meat? Is siskur-dah still an issue for them? How does their harmony work? Do they use it at all? What counts a &quot;one dot gift&quot; under then new system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:25:46-07:00","id":510695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508314-not-enough-werewolves-game-idea#post508314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -Allow the WB with a corresponding tell the ability to cast Wolf Rites<br /> -Allow Supernatural Merits to the WB<br /> -Give free Auspice and Tribe merits to the WB<br /> -Allow buying Shadow Gifts to the WB after a succesful hunt<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Everything but the gift idea is basically assigning free XP to them. <br /> <br /> Don't assign gifts to them the same way Uratha get them. Instead, let spirits give them the supernatural merits after a hunt and the required XP expenditure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T08:36:09-07:00","id":510724,"title":"","content":"How is &quot;allowing [STUFF]&quot; giving them free XP? (excluding the free merit one, that I understand)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:45:12-07:00","id":511143,"title":"","content":"<b>-Give free Auspice and Tribe merits to the WB</b><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T14:50:22-07:00","id":511174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508314-not-enough-werewolves-game-idea?p=511143#post511143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>-Give free Auspice and Tribe merits to the WB</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Reading comprehension is a vital skill.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508314-not-enough-werewolves-game-idea?p=510695#post510695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Everything</b> but the gift idea is basically assigning free XP to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/508314-not-enough-werewolves-game-idea?p=510724#post510724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How is &quot;allowing [STUFF]&quot; giving them free XP? (<b>excluding the free merit one, that I understand</b>)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:39:33-07:00","id":511250,"title":"","content":"Let's make things clear.<br /> <br /> A) I read that every idea I had (except the one based on Gifts, powers of the Uratha) was basically giving free XP to my players<br /> B) I asked how come (except for the idea where I was giving free merits to my players, because that's definitelly extra XP)<br /> C) ???<br /> D) I'm being told giving away free merits is giving free XP<br /> <br /> I think I understand that giving free merits is not something people like. Fine. I like the idea that successful hunts give access to supernatural merits fitting to the spirit being hunted rather than Gifts (Uratha powers), and I might toy around with this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T16:45:40-07:00","id":511303,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's anything wrong with free xp. 10 xp would be roughly equivalent to the free renown/gifts that Uratha start with.<br /> <br /> I'd offer them a couple extra tells. Including maybe some custom made ones if they feel limited by the options.<br /> <br /> I think the free Auspice/Tribe Wolf Blood merits make a lot of sense as well.<br /> <br /> Then maybe access to one or two gifts. With either no renown modifier (to represent their limited capability), or the renown modifier being equal to the number of facets they have in said gift (to demonstrate their mastery of the gift). I'd probably go with two gifts max, as they would have a limited capacity for spirit gifts being carved into them. Maybe represent them as tattoos. They would have to really work to acquire those gifts. Gifts would all cost 1-2 willpower to use and might be modified in other ways to make sense for the wolf blooded. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T16:03:54-07:00","id":512379,"title":"","content":"Hum, I don't get why &quot;giving free XP to players&quot; is not a good thing when you have a bunch of <i>weaker </i>wolf-blooded <i>sitting next to other players at the same table</i> playing full werewolves. I mean, <i>of course</i> you should give them something equivalent and different for it to be worth their while ! :P A starting werewolf gets a ton of free stuff.<br /> <br /> I mean, to compare with VtR: it would be like having ghoul players sitting next to Vampire players and not giving them something nice in exchange for basically gimping themselves. Except, it's even <i>more so</i> for the wolf-blooded who don't even have, by default, disciplines to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5602-barbechenue","name":"BarbeChenue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"80"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T03:27:07-07:00","id":512788,"title":"","content":"The one Wolf-Blooded PC in my game, we decided he's basically a very, very strong manifestation of Wolf-Bloodedness. He has three Tells. I also lumped something like 30 or 35 Experiences on him too.<br /> <br /> It's worked pretty well so far.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}